{% block title %}AC11.01 – Multimeter Skills{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <div class="container">

        <h1>AC11.01 – Measuring Voltage, Current and Resistance</h1>
        <p><strong>Objective:</strong> Master the use of a multimeter to measure voltage, current, and resistance in an electrical circuit.</p>

        <hr>

        <h2>Reflective Analysis</h2>
        <p>
            This activity helped me understand the importance of electrical safety and the correct use of measuring instruments.
            I learned how to select the appropriate function and range on the multimeter, how to take accurate measurements
            without disturbing the circuit, and how to critically interpret the results.
            This activity strengthened my practical skills in electronics and reinforced my theoretical knowledge such as Ohm’s Law.
        </p>

        <h2>Evidence Documents</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Photos showing the multimeter measuring voltage, current, and resistance.</li>
            <li>Diagram of the circuit used for the measurements.</li>
            <li>Measurement report showing expected and obtained values with comments on possible discrepancies.</li>
        </ul>

